/-
Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/K14/Thread2Full.lean: OVER ANY TERM O of Others
(Honest/K14/Thread2.lean), the term that has this kind's own four fields laid: the kind's six
halves, the sendings' own tables as the thread's tables, and what an honest prover holds as
Honest/K14/Holds2.lean lays it. At it, UNDER A PREMISE ON THE PLAN Q, the premises ON THESE FOUR
FIELDS (hs, table, fixed, holds) that this kind's laws take hold TOGETHER, whatever O's other fields
are. The premise on the plan: that the shape splits the row (Fold) (Q.S.sharedSplitNeeded = true:
halvesIn_full, halfIn_full); that the kind's eight are made (flat_counts, trees_b2); or Plan2, which
gives both (treesU_full, treesO_full, atSend_full, exchange_full, exchange8_full, plays_full,
fits_full, accepted_full, accepted_keys). sendsIn_full has no premise. The premises on O's other
fields stay premises: that no two messages have one tenant (O.N: exchange_full, exchange8_full); the
columns, the key and the seeds at the inputs that count (O.stored, O.valid: plays_full,
accepted_full).
IT IS NO LAYER OVER O: it writes over O.hs WHOLE (whatever halves O had for the proximity tests and
the closing are gone), over O.fixed at EVERY source, over O.table at EVERY tree of the chain's own,
and over O.holds. What stays O's: the committed table (stored), the inputs that count (valid), the
planner's chains, the lists of the proximity tests' and the closing's sub-protocols, the numbers,
the items' other meanings, table at the trees taken from another chain, the witness's type with its
lens (lens), what the witness holds beside this kind's words (rest), and the fields shape,
nothingLeft, n₁, n₂, keeps and rides.

  planData        the kind's public data at a plan: the point is the chain's round number 0, zeta
                  its round number 6
  treesU          how many trees "send o_u" states; where withU returns nothing the count is taken
                  at the empty array of notices
  fullOver        **the term**: { O with hs, fixed, table, holds }: hs: the kind's four halves and
                  the two sendings' halves; fixed: every tree is fixed by the first challenge;
                  table: at the chain's first treesU trees the tables of "send o_u", behind them
                  those of "send o_omega"; holds: holds2
  halvesIn_full, sendsIn_full   the facts on the halves (HalvesIn, SendsIn); the first where the
                  shape splits the row (Fold)
  halfIn_full     HalfIn at both sendings, where the shape splits the row (Fold)
  flat_counts     the trees and rounds in front of the two sendings, in a list that begins as the
                  shared chain's
  trees_b2        what "send o_u" states of trees, at the eight
  treesU_full, treesO_full   TreesLaid at the members number 2 and 5, under Plan2
  atSend_full     AtSend at both, under Plan2
  exchange_full   Exchange at both sendings, from Plan2, SendShapes and that no two messages have
                  one tenant
  bookSplitFits, book_of_fits, exchange8_full   a public test on the book's entries (there is one,
                  and each is right); the sentence that it gives; Exchange at "SPLIT"
                  (exchange8_book, Honest/K14/Holds2.lean, applied), from Plan2, the tenants and
                  that test
  plays_full, fits_full, accepted_full   plays2, fits2 and accepted_all (Honest/K14/Plays2.lean,
                  AcceptedAll.lean), applied: all three under Plan2; plays_full and accepted_full
                  beside under their premises on O.stored and O.valid
  keysOver, accepted_keys   AN INSTANCE: over any O, the inputs that count are LAID as those whose
                  key fits and has no seed with the factor 0: there accepted_full's two premises on
                  valid hold, because valid is laid so: it shows that they can hold together with
                  the rest; IT DOES NOT MEET THEM (see below)
  accepted_at_key, accepted_at_real   accepted_keys joined with plan2_key and plan2_real
                  (Honest/K14/Thread2Member.lean): Accepted at the members 1 to 8 at the two typed
                  shapes, at every fall, at that instance of valid

WHAT THESE SENTENCES ARE WORTH HANGS ON O. Exchange, Plays and Accepted are sentences UNDER the
thread's sentence Thr. Where O.stored has no column for "LOC" to read, Thr holds at no stand from
the border number 5 on, and every such sentence at a member from 5 on holds for nothing. So stored
and valid are O's here, and plays_full takes as a premise that stored has the columns at the inputs
that count. THAT Thr HOLDS AT ANY STAND OF ANY SUCH THREAD IS SHOWN NOWHERE.
halvesIn_full, halfIn_full, flat_counts, trees_b2, treesU_full, treesO_full and atSend_full are
sentences on fields, not under Thr.
ON valid. By the frame's own rule of use (Honest/Thread/Thr.lean, its head on the field valid) an
implication from valid to a fact on the key, the seeds or the stored table is owed from the
committer's make, at every coin and seed, and is never met by laying the fact into valid. keysOver
lays it so. So accepted_keys, accepted_at_key and accepted_at_real are instances; the two premises
of accepted_full (hkey, hseeds) and that of plays_full (hcol) are met in no file of this library.
NO THEOREM OF THIS LIBRARY APPLIES exchange8_full. ITS THREE PREMISES STAND TOGETHER AS FIELDS OF
K14Asks (plan, tenant, book: the third as the sentence on the book's entries that the test gives;
Honest/K14/Asks.lean), FROM WHICH k14_asks APPLIES THE SAME LAW, exchange8_book; asks_key
(E2E/KeyAsksKey.lean; NOT IN FRONT OF A LAW OVER COINS) HAS K14Asks AT THE KEY's SHARED THREAD WITH
THE TENANTS' PREMISE, AMONG OTHERS, LEFT. EACH OF THE THREE IS PROVED, THE FIRST TWO AT THE KEY
FILE's WRITTEN PLAN QK: Plan2 QK sentUF layO for some layO, with no premise (plan2_full,
E2E/KeyShapeSharedTies.lean); bookSplitFits (keyBook K) QK = true at every K that fullPub returns
(book_asked, E2E/KeyBookSplit.lean); no two messages have one tenant at idleNm, a value of O.N's
type (idleNm_tenant, E2E/KeyStandFull.lean). Under the hypothesis P5J.AtMgA, Plan2 holds at qAt Zp
Np (plan2_sentWithU, Honest/K14/AsksAtShared.lean), and where onlineProverFromPublicFiles returns A, bookSplitFits A.B
(qAt Zp Np) = true (bookSplitFits_at_made, AtFullSide/K14/BookSplitAtMade.lean). Plan2 is shown as
well at the two typed shapes (Honest/K14/Thread2Member.lean). Lean's kernel evaluates bookSplitFits
at the key file's book at the written sizes, where it accepts, and at two changed copies, where it
refuses (book_full, book_bent, book_empty, E2E/KeyBookSplit.lean). No theorem puts it to the written
short list (writtenShort, Honest/K14/SharedAheadWritten.lean), though the entry of it that spends
the second sending's coins is named (behind_omega_named, Honest/K14/SharedAheadOwners.lean).

Limits. That a proof's sizes at the release's files are the typed ones is not claimed. Nothing on a
verifier's decision, on soundness or on hiding.
-/
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K14.SendingsShowsAt
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K14.Plays2

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

namespace ProofFile.Honest.K14
open OnBytes OnBytes.Params OnBytes.Params.Prices OnBytes.Plan Johnson.G
open VerifiableInference.Desc.K1 (realSized)
open Lk6.AtPlan (keyFull)
open VerifiableInference.Desc (Block)
open VerifiableInference.Desc.Own (keyFits)
open Desc.K14 (P14 St blocks frontBlock)
open Desc.K14.Honest

variable {Bk : ProverCoinCounts} {W₀ Rc X₀ P₁ Wt : Type} {Q : P14} {sentU : Array OracleNotice} {layO : TreeLay}

/-- The kind's public data at a plan: the plan's shape; the point is the chain's round number 0,
zeta its round number 6. -/
def planData (Q : P14) : Data := { S := Q.S, atPoint := 0, atZeta := 6 }

/-- How many trees "send o_u" states. Where withU returns nothing the count is taken at the empty
array of notices (getD #[]). That it is what the member states is shown where the kind's eight are
made (trees_b2). -/
def treesU (Q : P14) : Nat :=
  (Desc.K14.oraclesOf Q.codes ((Desc.K14.withU Q.S).getD #[]) [[0], []]).length

/-- **Over any O: the kind's six halves, the sendings' tables and holds2.** It writes over O.hs
whole, over O.fixed at every source (1), over O.table at every tree of the chain's own, and over
O.holds; every other field is O's. -/
noncomputable def fullOver (O : Others Bk W₀ Rc X₀ P₁ Wt) (Q : P14) (weights : W₀ → Weights)
    (rand : Rc → TableRand) : Others Bk W₀ Rc X₀ P₁ Wt :=
  { O with
    hs := proverSidesOfSharedRounds (planData Q) weights ++ proverSidesOfSharedSendings ⟨Q, 0⟩ weights rand
    table := fun σ =>
      match σ with
      | .own n =>
        if n < treesU Q then sendTable (jobU ⟨Q, 0⟩) (witOf Q weights rand) (sendPlace 2) 1 n
        else sendTable (jobOmega ⟨Q, 0⟩) (witOf Q weights rand) (sendPlace 5) 1 (n - treesU Q)
      | .taken a b => O.table (.taken a b)
    fixed := fun _ => 1
    holds := holds2 Q weights rand }

variable (O : Others Bk W₀ Rc X₀ P₁ Wt) (weights : W₀ → Weights) (rand : Rc → TableRand)

/-- **The facts on the halves, where the shape splits the row (Fold) (h2).** -/
theorem halvesIn_full (Q : P14) (h2 : Q.S.sharedSplitNeeded = true) :
    HalvesIn Q (fullOver O Q weights rand) (planData Q) weights := by
  refine ⟨rfl, ?_, fun h hh => List.mem_append_left _ hh⟩
  show ((proverSidesOfSharedRounds (planData Q) weights ++ proverSidesOfSharedSendings ⟨Q, 0⟩ weights rand :
    List (Placed Empty (Common W₀ Rc TableKey) X₀)).map (·.place)).Nodup
  rw [halves_eq, sendHalves_eq]
  have e : (planData Q).S.sharedSplitNeeded = true := h2
  rw [e, if_pos rfl]
  show ([place 1, place 4, place 7, place 8, sendPlace 2, sendPlace 5] :
    List VerifiableInference.Desc.Place).Nodup
  decide

/-- The two sendings' halves are among them. -/
theorem sendsIn_full (Q : P14) :
    SendsIn Q (fullOver O Q weights rand) (planData Q) weights rand :=
  fun _ hg => List.mem_append_right _ hg

/-- **HalfIn at both sendings, where the shape splits the row (Fold) (h2).** -/
theorem halfIn_full (Q : P14) (h2 : Q.S.sharedSplitNeeded = true) :
    HalfIn (fullOver O Q weights rand) (sendPlace 2) (jobU ⟨Q, 0⟩) (witOf Q weights rand) ∧
      HalfIn (fullOver O Q weights rand) (sendPlace 5) (jobOmega ⟨Q, 0⟩)
        (witOf Q weights rand) := by
  have H := halvesIn_full O weights rand Q h2
  constructor
  · exact find_of_mem _ { place := sendPlace 2, parts := _ } H.apart
      (sendsIn_full O weights rand Q _ (by rw [sendHalves_eq]; exact List.mem_cons_self ..))
  · exact find_of_mem _ { place := sendPlace 5, parts := _ } H.apart
      (sendsIn_full O weights rand Q _ (by
        rw [sendHalves_eq]
        exact List.mem_cons_of_mem _ (List.mem_cons_self ..)))

/-- **The trees and rounds in front of the two sendings.** -/
theorem flat_counts {Cl : Type} {xs : List (Block St Cl)} {c : Model.Verify.Chains}
    {b1 b2 b3 b4 b5 b6 b7 b8 : Block St Unit} (F : FlatOf xs c b1 b2 b3 b4 b5 b6 b7 b8)
    (hb : blocks Q = some [b1, b2, b3, b4, b5, b6, b7, b8]) :
    treesTo xs 2 = 0 ∧ treesTo xs 5 = (b2.oracles.flatMap id).length ∧ 1 ≤ roundsTo xs 2 ∧
      1 ≤ roundsTo xs 5 := by
  obtain ⟨x0, x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6, x7, x8, tl, rfl, l0, l1, l2, l3, l4, l5, l6, l7, l8⟩ := F
  obtain ⟨-, -, -, r1, o1, -, o4, -, -⟩ := declares3 Q b1 b2 b3 b4 b5 b6 b7 b8 hb
  obtain ⟨-, o3, -, -, -⟩ := declares_none Q b1 b2 b3 b4 b5 b6 b7 b8 hb
  have o0 : x0.oracles = [] := l0.oracles
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · simp [treesTo, o0, l1.oracles, o1]
  · simp [treesTo, o0, l1.oracles, o1, l2.oracles, l3.oracles, o3, l4.oracles, o4]
  · simp [roundsTo, declsTo, l1.rounds, r1]
  · simp [roundsTo, declsTo, l1.rounds, r1]
    omega

/-- What "send o_u" states of trees, at the eight. -/
theorem trees_b2 {b1 b2 b3 b4 b5 b6 b7 b8 : Block St Unit}
    (hb : blocks Q = some [b1, b2, b3, b4, b5, b6, b7, b8]) :
    (b2.oracles.flatMap id).length = treesU Q := by
  obtain ⟨sU, hU, rfl, -⟩ := Desc.K14.Law.two_sendings Q b1 b2 b3 b4 b5 b6 b7 b8 hb
  unfold treesU
  rw [hU]
  show ([Desc.K14.oraclesOf Q.codes
    (Desc.K14.parK1 Q 2 "o_u and the first mask" sU).sent [[0], []], []].flatMap id).length = _
  rw [Desc.K14.Law.parK1_sent]
  simp

/-- **TreesLaid at "send o_u", under Plan2.** -/
theorem treesU_full (hQ : Plan2 Q sentU layO) (Cl : Type) :
    TreesLaid (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread 2 (jobU ⟨Q, 0⟩)
      (witOf Q weights rand) := by
  obtain ⟨B⟩ := hQ.eight
  have F := flatOf_carried (Cl := Cl) O.c Q B.b1 B.b2 B.b3 B.b4 B.b5 B.b6 B.b7 B.b8 O.tests O.last
    B.made
  obtain ⟨t2, -, r2, -⟩ := flat_counts F B.made
  obtain ⟨-, pU, -, -⟩ := send_declares Q 0 B.b1 B.b2 B.b3 B.b4 B.b5 B.b6 B.b7 B.b8 B.made
  refine ⟨fun blk _ i _ => ⟨?_, jobU_readsBelow ⟨Q, 0⟩⟩, fun blk hblk i hi => ?_⟩
  · show 1 ≤ 0 + roundsTo _ 2
    rw [Nat.zero_add]
    exact r2
  · have L := F.at2 hblk
    rw [L.oracles, trees_b2 B.made] at hi
    have t2' : treesTo (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread.bs 2 = 0 := t2
    show (fullOver O Q weights rand).table (.own (treesTo _ 2 + i)) = _
    rw [t2', Nat.zero_add, L.place, pU]
    show (if i < treesU Q then _ else _) = _
    rw [if_pos hi]
    rfl

/-- **TreesLaid at "send o_omega", under Plan2.** -/
theorem treesO_full (hQ : Plan2 Q sentU layO) (Cl : Type) :
    TreesLaid (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread 5 (jobOmega ⟨Q, 0⟩)
      (witOf Q weights rand) := by
  obtain ⟨B⟩ := hQ.eight
  have F := flatOf_carried (Cl := Cl) O.c Q B.b1 B.b2 B.b3 B.b4 B.b5 B.b6 B.b7 B.b8 O.tests O.last
    B.made
  obtain ⟨-, t5, -, r5⟩ := flat_counts F B.made
  obtain ⟨-, -, -, pO⟩ := send_declares Q 0 B.b1 B.b2 B.b3 B.b4 B.b5 B.b6 B.b7 B.b8 B.made
  refine ⟨fun blk _ i _ => ⟨?_, jobOmega_readsBelow ⟨Q, 0⟩⟩, fun blk hblk i _ => ?_⟩
  · show 1 ≤ 0 + roundsTo _ 5
    rw [Nat.zero_add]
    exact r5
  · have L := F.at5 hblk
    have t5' : treesTo (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread.bs 5 = treesU Q :=
      t5.trans (trees_b2 B.made)
    show (fullOver O Q weights rand).table (.own (treesTo _ 5 + i)) = _
    rw [t5', L.place, pO]
    show (if treesU Q + i < treesU Q then _ else _) = _
    rw [if_neg (by omega), Nat.add_sub_cancel_left]
    rfl

/-- **AtSend at both sendings, under Plan2.** -/
theorem atSend_full (hQ : Plan2 Q sentU layO) (Cl : Type) :
    AtSend (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread 2 (jobU ⟨Q, 0⟩)
        (witOf Q weights rand) ∧
      AtSend (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread 5 (jobOmega ⟨Q, 0⟩)
        (witOf Q weights rand) := by
  obtain ⟨B⟩ := hQ.eight
  have H := halvesIn_full O weights rand Q hQ.facts.two
  have E := atEight2 B sentU Cl H
  have tU : TreesLaid (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread (1 + 1)
      (jobU ⟨Q, (planData Q).atPoint⟩) (witOf Q weights rand) := treesU_full O weights rand hQ Cl
  have tO : TreesLaid (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread (1 + 4)
      (jobOmega ⟨Q, (planData Q).atPoint⟩) (witOf Q weights rand) :=
    treesO_full O weights rand hQ Cl
  have aU := atSendU_of E (sendsIn_full O weights rand Q) tU
  have aO := atSendOmega_of E (sendsIn_full O weights rand Q) tO
  exact ⟨aU, aO⟩

/-- **Exchange at both sendings, from Plan2, SendShapes and that no two messages have one tenant.**
UNDER Thr: see the head. -/
theorem exchange_full (hQ : Plan2 Q sentU layO) (hSh : SendShapes Q)
    (hN : Function.Injective O.N.tenant) (Cl : Type) :
    Exchange (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread 2 ∧
      Exchange (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread 5 := by
  obtain ⟨hU, hO⟩ := halfIn_full O weights rand Q hQ.facts.two
  exact ⟨exchange2_of hQ _ Cl hN weights rand hU rfl hSh,
    exchange5_of hQ _ Cl hN weights rand hO rfl hSh⟩

/-- **A public test on the book**: there is an entry by which the part at "SPLIT" spends coins (its
spender is that part and its field once is true: in the frame's words the run is spent there, not
carried); every such entry names the second sending's part as the owner, and starts at o_sp's first
coin. Of an entry's name and count nothing is asked. -/
def bookSplitFits (Bk : ProverCoinCounts) (Q : P14) : Bool :=
  (Bk.ahead.any fun e => e.spender == ⟨place 8, 0⟩ && e.once) &&
    Bk.ahead.all fun e => !(e.spender == ⟨place 8, 0⟩ && e.once) ||
      (e.owner == ⟨sendPlace 5, 0⟩ && e.start == ⟨0, offsetOf (jobOmega ⟨Q, 0⟩).Q.codes
        (jobOmega ⟨Q, 0⟩).Q.sent (jobOmega ⟨Q, 0⟩).sort 1⟩)

/-- Where the book passes the test, the sentence on its entries that exchange8_book takes holds.
(That sentence alone is met by a book without such an entry too; the test asks for one.) -/
theorem book_of_fits {Bk : ProverCoinCounts} {Q : P14} (hB : bookSplitFits Bk Q = true) :
    ∀ e ∈ Bk.ahead, e.spender = ⟨place 8, 0⟩ → e.once = true →
      e.owner = ⟨sendPlace 5, 0⟩ ∧ e.start = ⟨0, offsetOf (jobOmega ⟨Q, 0⟩).Q.codes
        (jobOmega ⟨Q, 0⟩).Q.sent (jobOmega ⟨Q, 0⟩).sort 1⟩ := by
  intro e he hs ho
  unfold bookSplitFits at hB
  rw [Bool.and_eq_true] at hB
  have h := List.all_eq_true.1 hB.2 e he
  rw [hs, ho] at h
  simpa using h

/-- **exchange8_book, applied**: Exchange at "SPLIT", under Plan2, where no two messages have one
tenant and the book passes the test. UNDER Thr: see the head. -/
theorem exchange8_full (hQ : Plan2 Q sentU layO) (hN : Function.Injective O.N.tenant) (Cl : Type)
    (hB : bookSplitFits Bk Q = true) :
    Exchange (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread 8 := by
  obtain ⟨B⟩ := hQ.eight
  have E := atEight2 B sentU Cl (halvesIn_full O weights rand Q hQ.facts.two)
  have hAt : AtSplit (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread (1 + 7) (planData Q)
      weights := atSplit_of E hQ.facts.two
  exact exchange8_book hQ (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl hN (planData Q) weights rand hAt rfl rfl
    rfl rfl (book_of_fits hB)

/-- **plays2, applied, under Plan2.** hcol: at the inputs that count the committed table has the
columns that "LOC" reads: a premise on O's own fields. UNDER Thr: see the head. -/
theorem plays_full (hQ : Plan2 Q sentU layO) (Cl : Type)
    (hcol : ∀ w, O.valid w → ∀ p < 2 ^ (Desc.K14.readsAtLoc Q.S.fold Q.item).sh.a,
      ∃ u, O.stored w (Desc.K14.readsAtLoc Q.S.fold Q.item).item p = some u ∧
        u.length = (Desc.K14.readsAtLoc Q.S.fold Q.item).sh.W) (b : Nat) (h1 : 1 ≤ b)
    (h8 : b ≤ 8) : Plays (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread b := by
  obtain ⟨p1, p2, p3, p4, p5, p6, p7, p8⟩ := plays2 hQ Cl
    (halvesIn_full O weights rand Q hQ.facts.two) (sendsIn_full O weights rand Q)
    (treesU_full O weights rand hQ Cl)
    (treesO_full O weights rand hQ Cl) hcol
  match b, h1, h8 with
  | 1, _, _ => exact p1
  | 2, _, _ => exact p2
  | 3, _, _ => exact p3
  | 4, _, _ => exact p4
  | 5, _, _ => exact p5
  | 6, _, _ => exact p6
  | 7, _, _ => exact p7
  | 8, _, _ => exact p8

/-- **fits2, applied, under Plan2.** A sentence on fields, not under Thr. -/
theorem fits_full (hQ : Plan2 Q sentU layO) (Cl : Type) (b : Nat) (h1 : 1 ≤ b) (h8 : b ≤ 8) :
    FitsAt (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread b := by
  obtain ⟨B⟩ := hQ.eight
  obtain ⟨f1, f2, f3, f4, f5, f6, f7, f8⟩ :=
    fits2 B sentU Cl (halvesIn_full O weights rand Q hQ.facts.two) (sendsIn_full O weights rand Q)
  match b, h1, h8 with
  | 1, _, _ => exact f1
  | 2, _, _ => exact f2
  | 3, _, _ => exact f3
  | 4, _, _ => exact f4
  | 5, _, _ => exact f5
  | 6, _, _ => exact f6
  | 7, _, _ => exact f7
  | 8, _, _ => exact f8

/-- **accepted_all, applied, under Plan2**: at every fall. hkey, hseeds: at the inputs that count
the key fits, and none of its seeds has the factor 0: premises on O's own field valid, spent at the
member number 3 alone. UNDER Thr: see the head. -/
theorem accepted_full (hQ : Plan2 Q sentU layO) (Cl : Type)
    (fall : Nat → St → List Fmt.Drawn → Option String) (b : Nat) (h1 : 1 ≤ b) (h8 : b ≤ 8)
    (hkey : b = 3 → ∀ w, O.valid w → keyFits w.key Q.par.S.fold.index = true)
    (hseeds : b = 3 → ∀ w, O.valid w → noZeroFactor w.key = true) :
    Accepted (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver O Q weights rand) Cl).thread fall b :=
  accepted_all hQ Cl (halvesIn_full O weights rand Q hQ.facts.two) (sendsIn_full O weights rand Q)
    fall b h1 h8 hkey hseeds

/-- An instance: over any O, the inputs that count are LAID as those whose key fits and has no seed
with the factor 0. -/
def keysOver (O : Others Bk W₀ Rc X₀ P₁ Wt) (Q : P14) : Others Bk W₀ Rc X₀ P₁ Wt :=
  { O with valid := fun w => keyFits w.key Q.par.S.fold.index = true ∧ noZeroFactor w.key = true }

/-- **accepted_full at that instance, under Plan2**: its two premises on valid hold there because
valid is laid so: they are not met by it: see the head, on valid. UNDER Thr: see the head. -/
theorem accepted_keys (hQ : Plan2 Q sentU layO) (Cl : Type)
    (fall : Nat → St → List Fmt.Drawn → Option String) (b : Nat) (h1 : 1 ≤ b) (h8 : b ≤ 8) :
    Accepted (letters2 Q sentU (fullOver (keysOver O Q) Q weights rand) Cl).thread fall b :=
  accepted_full (keysOver O Q) weights rand hQ Cl fall b h1 h8 (fun _ _ h => h.1)
    fun _ _ h => h.2

/-- **Accepted at a typed shape**: at the typed sizes of a key of full size, at the sentU that goes
out with o_u at that shape (withU: it binds sentU to the letter), at every item and every list
beforePoint that is not empty: at every fall, over every O, at valid laid as in keysOver: an
instance: see the head, on valid. UNDER Thr: see the head. -/
theorem accepted_at_key : ∃ sentU : Array OracleNotice,
    Desc.K14.withU keyFull.once.shape = some sentU ∧
    ∀ (item : Nat) (bp : List (Nat × Nat)), bp ≠ [] → ∀ (Cl : Type)
      (fall : Nat → St → List Fmt.Drawn → Option String) (b : Nat), 1 ≤ b → b ≤ 8 →
      Accepted (letters2 ⟨recordSet, .once, keyFull.codes, keyFull.once.shape, item, bp⟩ sentU
        (fullOver (keysOver O ⟨recordSet, .once, keyFull.codes, keyFull.once.shape, item, bp⟩)
          ⟨recordSet, .once, keyFull.codes, keyFull.once.shape, item, bp⟩ weights rand)
        Cl).thread fall b := by
  obtain ⟨sentU, layO, hp⟩ := plan2_key
  exact ⟨sentU, (hp 0 [(0, 0)] (List.cons_ne_nil _ _)).facts.goes,
    fun item bp hbp Cl fall b h1 h8 =>
    accepted_keys O weights rand (hp item bp hbp) Cl fall b h1 h8⟩

/-- **The like at the typed sizes over a proof file's own codes**, at the sentU that goes out with
o_u at that shape (withU), at every item and every list beforePoint that is not empty: an instance
too. -/
theorem accepted_at_real : ∃ (x : LinSized) (sentU : Array OracleNotice),
    realSized = some (x, codesFull2) ∧ Desc.K14.withU x.shape = some sentU ∧
    ∀ (item : Nat) (bp : List (Nat × Nat)), bp ≠ [] → ∀ (Cl : Type)
      (fall : Nat → St → List Fmt.Drawn → Option String) (b : Nat), 1 ≤ b → b ≤ 8 →
      Accepted (letters2 ⟨recordSet, .shared, codesFull2, x.shape, item, bp⟩ sentU
        (fullOver (keysOver O ⟨recordSet, .shared, codesFull2, x.shape, item, bp⟩)
          ⟨recordSet, .shared, codesFull2, x.shape, item, bp⟩ weights rand) Cl).thread fall b := by
  obtain ⟨x, sentU, layO, hx, hp⟩ := plan2_real
  exact ⟨x, sentU, hx, (hp 0 [(0, 0)] (List.cons_ne_nil _ _)).facts.goes,
    fun item bp hbp Cl fall b h1 h8 =>
    accepted_keys O weights rand (hp item bp hbp) Cl fall b h1 h8⟩

